<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Standing civilization-scale directives (system 12: the god layer, docs/spec/simworld-spec.md §10).
    RimWorld has nothing to port here — the player drafts individual colonists there rather than issuing
    directives a whole civilization keeps obeying — so this is SimWorld's own translation, spread across the
    era ladder (EraDefs/EraDefs.xml) the same way research is. Every edict costs public mood while active
    (moodThought), which is the "demanding hard things should cost public mood" half of the brief; most rely
    on the base EdictWorker for everything declarative (prioritizedWork, researchFocus, moodThought all read
    live off this def), except GreatWorksMandate, which exercises the Class= worker seam for something a def
    field can't express on its own — see EdictWorker_ExemptMinors.

    HuntersMandate carries obsoleteEra: entering the Bronze age is a civilization that has learned to farm and
    to store, at which point a mandate that pulls every hand into the hunt stops being the thing to demand —
    GodManager retires it on its own the moment that era is entered (see EdictDef.obsoleteEra and GodManager's
    era-transition handler). It lasts through the Agrarian age, while the first fields are still uncertain.

    The two exclusive edicts are bursts, not standing orders (era progression, 2026-11-24): each lasts a few days
    (durationDays) and then rests (cooldownDays), so "nothing else gets done" is a decision about this week
    rather than a setting left on. The roster across the eras, and what each edict grounds in, is
    docs/design/era-progression.md section 3.

    GreatWorksMandate is also the one edict carrying prioritizedConstruction (building.initiative): "quarry
    and building site before anything else" is exactly SettlementConstructionInitiative's own construction
    bias, not just its WorkGiver push — a settlement under this mandate builds its walls and storage before
    anything else it might otherwise have queued.
  -->

  <EdictDef>
    <defName>HuntersMandate</defName>
    <label>hunter's mandate</label>
    <description>For three days every able hand goes out after game, and every animal on the land is marked for the hunt. The band eats, but nothing else gets done until they come home.</description>
    <requiredEra>SticksAndStones</requiredEra>
    <obsoleteEra>Bronze</obsoleteEra>
    <durationDays>3</durationDays>
    <cooldownDays>7</cooldownDays>
    <researchFocus>Hunting</researchFocus>
    <!-- "Nothing else gets done": every able hand hunts first, past the food gate (EdictDef.exclusiveWork). -->
    <exclusiveWork>true</exclusiveWork>
    <prioritizedWork>
      <li>Hunting</li>
    </prioritizedWork>
    <moodThought>UnderHuntersMandate</moodThought>
  </EdictDef>

  <EdictDef>
    <defName>BreakTheSod</defName>
    <label>break the sod</label>
    <description>For ten days every able hand works the fields: sowing, tending and bringing in the harvest, whatever else waits.</description>
    <requiredEra>Agrarian</requiredEra>
    <durationDays>10</durationDays>
    <cooldownDays>20</cooldownDays>
    <researchFocus>Agriculture</researchFocus>
    <!-- "Whatever else waits": every able hand sows first (EdictDef.exclusiveWork). -->
    <exclusiveWork>true</exclusiveWork>
    <prioritizedWork>
      <li>Growing</li>
    </prioritizedWork>
    <moodThought>UnderBreakTheSod</moodThought>
  </EdictDef>

  <EdictDef>
    <defName>GreatWorksMandate</defName>
    <label>great works mandate</label>
    <description>Quarry and building site before anything else, and walls and storehouses before anything else is built. Children are spared the mandate's cost, but not its labor shortage.</description>
    <requiredEra>Bronze</requiredEra>
    <researchFocus>Masonry</researchFocus>
    <prioritizedWork>
      <li>Construction</li>
      <li>Mining</li>
    </prioritizedWork>
    <prioritizedConstruction>
      <li>Wall</li>
      <li>StorageHut</li>
    </prioritizedConstruction>
    <workerClass>SimWorld.God.EdictWorker_ExemptMinors</workerClass>
    <!-- offices.edicts: a settlement's public works are the stewardship's own business (Roles_Offices.xml
         emphasizes Construction for it), so a mandate to put them first needs a seated steward to drive it.
         With none seated anywhere it cannot be issued, and a standing one is suspended until one is. The
         eldership is never named here: it retires for good, and an edict gated on it would end with it. -->
    <requiredOffice>Steward</requiredOffice>
    <moodThought>UnderGreatWorksMandate</moodThought>
  </EdictDef>

  <EdictDef>
    <defName>IronDiscipline</defName>
    <label>iron discipline</label>
    <description>The forge does not go cold. Smithing comes before every other kind of work.</description>
    <requiredEra>Medieval</requiredEra>
    <researchFocus>Steel</researchFocus>
    <prioritizedWork>
      <li>Smithing</li>
    </prioritizedWork>
    <moodThought>UnderIronDiscipline</moodThought>
  </EdictDef>

  <EdictDef>
    <defName>IndustrialMobilization</defName>
    <label>industrial mobilization</label>
    <description>The whole town tools up: crafting and hauling come before every other kind of work.</description>
    <requiredEra>Industrial</requiredEra>
    <researchFocus>SteamEngine</researchFocus>
    <prioritizedWork>
      <li>Crafting</li>
      <li>Hauling</li>
    </prioritizedWork>
    <moodThought>UnderIndustrialMobilization</moodThought>
  </EdictDef>

</Defs>
